          "title": "Night shift",
          "text": "Marina has worked night shifts at a hospital for five years. 'At first it was terrible,' she says. 'I couldn't get used to sleeping during the day — every noise woke me up. I used to drink four coffees a night just to stay awake.' Now she has blackout curtains, earplugs and a strict routine. 'I'm used to it now. Actually, I like the quiet of the hospital at 3 a.m. But my body will never be completely used to it.'",
